## The Origins of Fleshy Findlay

**Series:** Behind the Fire

**Story:** Fleshy Findlay

---

# Every Story Begins Somewhere

For **Fleshy Findlay**, it began with a mask.

In August 2018, shortly after purchasing our small three-season cabin in Québec's Laurentians, we discovered this unusual hand-painted mask tucked away inside.

No one knew who had made it.

No one knew why it had been left behind.

Yet from the moment I first saw it, I felt as though it had a story waiting to be told.

---

# The Spark

For years, this mask has remained mounted inside our cabin.

I've told versions of its story around campfires with my nieces and nephews, rewritten it countless times, and watched it slowly evolve into the story readers know today as *Fleshy Findlay*.


---

# The Real Story Behind the Story

One of the goals of the **Behind the Fire** series is to share where Campfire Horror Tales truly begin.

Every story starts with a real photograph, a memory capturing some "spark", a thing that starts the process and evolves into something deeper, darker, and well yes, creepy.

This mask is still hanging in our cabin today.

It remains one of my favourite reminders that the best stories often begin with a curious thought...and a wild imagination.

---

# Original Photograph

The inset photograph featured with this article is the original image taken at our family cabin in the Laurentians.

It remains one of the earliest pieces of inspiration behind Campfire Horror Tales.

